    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Yordan Alvarez** (75.69) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.22) anchor the lineup as our most efficient starts. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in asset, leveraging an elite .421 xwOBA against Jack Leiter; despite a neutral park, his skill gap is simply too wide to ignore. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns a significant boost from an exploitable matchup against Sean Burke. While his spot in the nine-hole typically suppresses his score, the 87% stolen base success rate against Burke\u2019s slow delivery makes him a high-upside play in a category where we remain aggressive. **Junior Caminero** (67.27) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) round out the top tier, with both benefiting from favorable SP skill profiles and positive dynamic platoon splits.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin** (52.36), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Kyle Schwarber** (52.46). Despite **Caleb Durbin** profiling as a potential spark plug, the optimizer prioritized the higher base projection and lineup security of **Kyle Schwarber**, despite his tough draw against Braxton Ashcraft. We are also monitoring the heavy-hitter stack of **Christian Yelich** (60.32) and **Gary Sanchez** (44.40); both benefit from favorable wind conditions today, which serves as a vital cushion against the threat of Joe Ryan\u2019s 3.41 xERA. **Colt Keith** (60.25) also warrants attention, as his elevated spot in the order combined with strong platoon metrics makes him a reliable start over the lower-floor options.\n\nRisk remains prevalent today, primarily due to the \"Lineup Pending\" status for almost all of our roster. We are currently projecting **Dillon Dingler** (42.19) and **Gary Sanchez** (44.40) based on historical order placement, but any downward shift in their batting position will likely render them sub-floor starts. Additionally, while **Zac Veen** remains safely tucked away in the minors, we must remain vigilant regarding the volatile matchups facing **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** against Braxton Ashcraft. We are maximizing our efficiency by leaning into volume and speed, but be prepared to shift bench assets like **Chase Meidroth** if late-breaking lineup news shifts our platoon advantages negatively.",
